      "text": "Language Family Nuances & Grammatical Highlights"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "• **Indo-European:** Features tense auxiliary verbs and person/number inflections.\n• **Turkic Family (Tatar, Bashkir, Chuvash):** Agglutinative suffix structures expressing tense and person without separate helper verbs.\n• **Kartvelian (Georgian):** Polypersonal verb agreement marking subject and indirect/direct objects."
